meta {
  name: receive requisition
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}requisitions/:id/receive/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: 2
}

body:json {
  {
    // Chamber to put the stock in: empty, or holding this component. Required.
    "location": "D11",

    // Quantity received. Optional, defaults to the requested quantity.
    "quantity": "5",

    // Actual amounts paid, BDT. Optional; overwrite the component's prices.
    "unit_price": "650.00",
    "delivery_charge": "100.00",

    // Optional; goes into the status history and the movement note.
    "note": "Invoice TS-10492",

    // ---- Only for free-text requisitions (creating the component) ----
    // Category id. Required for free-text requisitions.
    "category": 7,

    // Optional. Name defaults to requested_part_name; part number must be unique.
    "part_number": "ESP32-DEVKITC-V4",
    "manufacturer": "Espressif",
    "minimum_quantity": "2"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  The receipt flow for an `ORDERED` requisition (FR-4.5). **Admin only**. In one
  transaction it:
  1. creates the library component, if the requisition was free text (needs `category`),
  2. adds the received quantity to `location` (an ADD movement noted "Received against REQ-..."),
  3. overwrites the component's last buying price and delivery charge with what was paid,
  4. marks the requisition `RECEIVED`.


  ## API example response
